---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
const EMAIL = 'tsouth2@gmail.com';
---
<Legal
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy | Family Bakery: Merge & Bake"
  heading="Family Bakery privacy"
  description="What Family Bakery: Merge & Bake keeps, what it sends, and what it never does."
  lastUpdated="October 10, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Family Bakery: Merge &amp; Bake is a merge game for Android and iPhone. It has no accounts, no ads,
    no analytics and no tracking. This policy covers the game only.
  </p>

  <h2>Your café stays on your phone</h2>
  <p>
    Your progress, settings and café are saved on your device. They are not uploaded anywhere. If you
    use Move my café in Settings, the café code is created on your phone and goes only where you paste it.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    The game sells one optional purchase that opens the whole café. Payment is handled by Google Play or
    the App Store; we never see your card or payment details. To confirm and restore the purchase, the game uses
    <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat</a>, which receives a random ID created by the app,
    your purchase records and basic technical details such as app version, device type and country. We use
    this only to unlock the game for you.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell or share your information, show ads, track you across apps or websites, or ask for your
    name, email, contacts, location, photos or microphone.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The game is meant for players 13 and over and does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Uninstalling the game deletes your café from the device. To delete the purchase records held by RevenueCat,
    email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. Your store account keeps its own purchase history.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date above changes with it. Questions can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
